            {
                "entry_id": "27243fd3-8dba-371b-8795-389fb41a7b6e",
                "word": "APL",
                "pos": "abbrev",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e7941ed-9fe6-3407-a712-500d544cbc57",
                        "entry_id": "27243fd3-8dba-371b-8795-389fb41a7b6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abkürzung von „Applied Physics Laboratory“ an der Johns Hopkins University"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "physics"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9f555ae-04b1-417b-ab9a-8b17f0ed9c81",
                                "sense_id": "8e7941ed-9fe6-3407-a712-500d544cbc57",
                                "text": "„Having traveled from the New Horizons spacecraft over 3.1 billion miles (five hours, eight minutes at light speed), the final item – a segment of a Pluto-Charon observation sequence taken by the Ralph/LEISA imager – arrived at mission operations at the Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory (APL) in Laurel, Maryland, at 5:48 a.m. EDT on Oct. 25.“",
                                "translation": "„Nach über 3,1 Milliarden Meilen (fünf Stunden [und] acht Minuten mit Lichtgeschwindigkeit) von der New-Horizons-Raumsonde kam das letzte Element – ein Segment einer Pluto-Charon-Beobachtungsfolge des Ralph/LEISA-Imagers – am Missionszentrum im Johns Hopkins Applied Physics Laboratory (APL) in Laurel, Maryland, um 5:48 Uhr EDT am 25. Oktober, an.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "83e722b5-81aa-3118-89aa-7db167c9f4de",
                        "entry_id": "27243fd3-8dba-371b-8795-389fb41a7b6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abkürzung von „Applied Physics Laboratory“ an der University of Washington"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "physics"
                        ],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "daafb33c-59c1-3ae4-818a-959f45d307f0",
                        "entry_id": "27243fd3-8dba-371b-8795-389fb41a7b6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abkürzung von „A Programming Language“ – nach dem Buch „A Programming Language“ benannte, 1962 erschienene Programmiersprache"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Programmiersprache"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b5724c5-c8df-4500-a7b5-a043a491758d",
                                "sense_id": "daafb33c-59c1-3ae4-818a-959f45d307f0",
                                "text": "„The mathematical notation for manipulating arrays which developed into the APL programming language was developed by Iverson at Harvard University starting in 1957, and published in his A Programming Language in 1962.“",
                                "translation": "„Die mathematische Schreibweise zum Manipulieren von Arrays, die man in die Programmiersprache APL einbrachte, wurde von Iverson an der Harvard University ab 1957 entwickelt und in seinem „A Programming Language“ 1962 veröffentlicht.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                    }
